Subject: Cantor Semantic Inspection Wire P0 Solution

@ [solution_uuid] 1ed87a64-d391-411c-916a-b3ec0728892e
@ [specification_uuid] 1bddf5c8-35b7-4b29-a833-921048a21410

& [Architecture]
  + cantor_sop_inspect_wire owns only outer machine forms raw bounds dispatch fault shaping response sealing and replay
  + respond first checks the raw bound then strictly decodes the envelope and calls cantor_sop_inspect inspect exactly once
  + every governed input or nested semantic fault becomes a refused WireResponse while internal serialization faults remain ordinary Result faults
  + validate_response strictly parses the supplied response and compares it with a complete deterministic respond replay

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + request data is profile operation and exact nested InspectionRequest
  + response data is profile capability operation status optional valid request_digest mutually exclusive result or fault non_authority and response_digest
  + success invariant is status succeeded result present fault absent and exact nested validation
  + refusal invariant is status refused result absent fault present with bounded code and UTF-8 message

& [MachineContract]
  + strict deny-unknown-field JSON accepts exactly one bounded value and rejects duplicate trailing malformed unsupported or excess bytes
  + request bound is MAX_REQUEST_MACHINE_BYTES plus65536 and response bound is MAX_RESULT_MACHINE_BYTES plus65536
  + stable struct field order and compact JSON produce deterministic bytes for identical requests

& [Faults]
  + wire_request_limit unsupported_wire invalid_json nested published inspection faults wire_response_limit wire_response_mismatch and internal serialization faults

& [NoEffects]
  + no io path fs env clock random thread net process database cache provider model operator or mutation input exists
